meta {
  name: 52 Bulk Set Recoverable (Discarded)
  type: http
  seq: 52
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/accession/order-samples/bulk/set-recoverable
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "ids": ["{{sampleId}}"],
    "isRecoverable": true,
    "skipInvalid": true,
    "notes": "Sample still in the tray"
  }
}

tests {
  test("flag set (or refused)", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.be.oneOf([200, 201, 422]);
  });
}

docs {
  Set the **recoverable** flag of **Discarded** samples (Sample Search popup). Retrieve out of Discarded
  is refused (`SAMPLE_RETRIEVE_BLOCKED_NOT_RECOVERABLE`) unless the flag is true. Editable while the
  sample stays Discarded; every change is logged on the history ("Recoverable changed: No → Yes").
  Permission: the same as Discard. All-or-nothing for the ids, unless `skipInvalid: true` (the Sample Search popup
  sends it): a sample that is no longer Discarded, or whose order is cancelled, is then left out and named in
  `skipped` (`id`, `accessionNo`, `reason`, `code`) while the others are still changed. A sample that already has the
  value is never an error (nothing is written). A missing id always fails the call.

  The popup sends ONLY the rows the button can change (Mark Recoverable: the rows that are not recoverable yet; Mark
  Not Recoverable: the recoverable ones), so a row another department marked differently is left alone. The server
  does not check the caller's departments for these ids (same as the other accession actions).

  `isRecoverable` must be a real JSON `true` / `false`: the text "false", `0`, `1` and so on are refused with 400
  `VALIDATION_ERROR` (they used to be turned into `true`).

  Errors (422): `SAMPLE_FLAG_NOT_ALLOWED` (a sample is not Discarded), `SAMPLE_ORDER_CANCELLED`.

  The Discard request (`14 Discard Sample`, bulk discard) also accepts `isRecoverable` (default false).
}
